# Step 1: Database Architecture for Parametric Estimator

## Background

We are pivoting from a **Manual BOM Builder** (manually adding line items) to a **Parametric Estimator** where:
1. User selects a **Template** (e.g., "iConiq Sliding Door 2-Panel") and a **Color**
2. User inputs **Width (W)** and **Height (H)** in millimeters
3. A **Formula Engine** evaluates template-linked formulas to produce a **Cutting List**
4. A **1D Bin Packing Algorithm** determines how many full-length bars (6000mm) are needed
5. Cost is based on **full bars purchased**, not just cut pieces

---

## Proposed Schema Design

### Architecture Overview

```mermaid
erDiagram
    Category ||--o{ Material : "has"
    Material ||--o{ MaterialVariant : "has"
    Color ||--o{ MaterialVariant : "for"
    
    Category ||--o{ ProductTemplate : "belongs to"
    ProductTemplate ||--o{ TemplateComponent : "has"
    TemplateComponent }o--|| Material : "uses"
    ProductTemplate ||--o{ TemplateAccessory : "includes"
    ProductTemplate ||--o| GlassSpecification : "has"
    
    EstimationProject ||--o{ CuttingResult : "produces"
    EstimationProject }o--|| ProductTemplate : "uses"
    EstimationProject }o--|| Color : "selected"
    CuttingResult }o--|| Material : "for"
```

### What We Keep (Untouched)

The existing **master data** models remain as-is — they are the backbone of the material catalog:

| Model | Purpose | Change |
|-------|---------|--------|
| `Category` | Brand/series grouping | No change |
| `Material` | Raw aluminum profile | No change |
| `MaterialVariant` | Color-specific pricing | No change |
| `Color` | Available colors | No change |

### What We Add (New Models)

#### 1. `ProductTemplate` — The Door/Window Model

```prisma
model ProductTemplate {
  id          String   @id @default(cuid())
  categoryId  String

  name        String   @unique   // "iConiq Sliding Door 2-Panel"
  slug        String   @unique   // "iconiq-sliding-2p"
  description String?
  imageUrl    String?            // diagram/schematic placeholder

  /// Default bar length for this template's optimization (mm)
  standardBarLengthMm  Int   @default(6000)

  sortOrder   Int      @default(0)
  isActive    Boolean  @default(true)

  createdAt DateTime @default(now())
  updatedAt DateTime @updatedAt

  category      Category             @relation(fields: [categoryId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
  components    TemplateComponent[]
  accessories   TemplateAccessory[]
  glass         GlassSpecification?
  projects      EstimationProject[]

  @@index([categoryId])
  @@map("product_templates")
}
```

> [!IMPORTANT]
> `standardBarLengthMm` defaults to 6000mm (standard aluminum bar length in Thailand). This can be overridden per template if specific profiles come in different stock lengths.

---

#### 2. `TemplateComponent` — Formula-Linked Profile Requirements

This is the **core of the parametric engine**. Each row defines:
- Which `Material` profile to use
- A **formula string** (e.g., `"H - 35"`, `"W / 2 + 10"`) evaluated against W and H
- The **quantity** of cuts needed

```prisma
model TemplateComponent {
  id         String @id @default(cuid())
  templateId String
  materialId String

  /// Human-readable label, e.g., "Jamb (Left)", "Top Track"
  label       String

  /// Math formula string evaluated with variables W and H.
  /// Examples: "H - 35", "W", "W / 2 + 10", "(W - 40) / 2"
  /// Supports: +, -, *, /, parentheses, integers, decimals, W, H
  formula     String

  /// Number of identical cuts produced by this formula
  /// e.g., quantity=2 means "cut 2 pieces at this length"
  quantity    Int    @default(1)

  /// Optional override for bar length (mm). If null, uses template default.
  barLengthMm Int?

  sortOrder   Int    @default(0)

  createdAt DateTime @default(now())
  updatedAt DateTime @updatedAt

  template  ProductTemplate @relation(fields: [templateId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
  material  Material        @relation(fields: [materialId], references: [id], onDelete: Restrict)

  @@index([templateId])
  @@index([materialId])
  @@map("template_components")
}
```

> [!NOTE]
> **Formula Safety**: We will NOT use `eval()`. Step 2 will implement a **safe parser** using a whitelist approach:
> - **Allowed tokens**: numbers, `W`, `H`, `+`, `-`, `*`, `/`, `(`, `)`
> - **Parser**: A simple recursive-descent parser or tokenizer that rejects any unrecognized token
> - **No function calls, no variable assignments, no string operations** — purely arithmetic

---

#### 3. `GlassSpecification` — Glass Area & Pricing per Template

```prisma
model GlassSpecification {
  id         String @id @default(cuid())
  templateId String @unique  // one glass spec per template

  /// Formula for glass width in mm (e.g., "W - 60")
  widthFormula   String
  /// Formula for glass height in mm (e.g., "H - 80")
  heightFormula  String

  /// Number of glass panels
  panelCount     Int     @default(1)

  /// Cost per square meter of glass (THB/m²)
  pricePerSqM    Float

  /// Glass type description, e.g., "6mm Clear Tempered"
  glassType      String  @default("6mm Clear")

  createdAt DateTime @default(now())
  updatedAt DateTime @updatedAt

  template ProductTemplate @relation(fields: [templateId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)

  @@map("glass_specifications")
}
```

> [!TIP]
> **Glass cost formula**: `glassCost = panelCount × (widthFormula(W,H) / 1000) × (heightFormula(W,H) / 1000) × pricePerSqM`
> This converts mm² to m² before applying the price.

---

#### 4. `TemplateAccessory` — Fixed Accessories per Template

```prisma
model TemplateAccessory {
  id         String @id @default(cuid())
  templateId String

  name        String    // "Roller Set", "Handle", "Lock", "Weatherstrip"
  quantity    Int       @default(1)
  unitCost    Float     // THB per piece
  unit        String    @default("piece")

  sortOrder   Int       @default(0)

  createdAt DateTime @default(now())
  updatedAt DateTime @updatedAt

  template ProductTemplate @relation(fields: [templateId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)

  @@index([templateId])
  @@map("template_accessories")
}
```

---

#### 5. Updated `EstimationProject` — Now Template-Driven

```prisma
model EstimationProject {
  id              String @id @default(cuid())

  /// Customer / project info
  projectName     String
  customerName    String?
  customerPhone   String?
  customerAddress String?
  notes           String?

  /// ─── PARAMETRIC INPUTS (NEW — now REQUIRED) ───
  templateId      String         // which door/window template
  colorId         String         // selected color for all profiles
  widthMm         Float          // user-input Width (W) in mm
  heightMm        Float          // user-input Height (H) in mm

  /// Pricing adjustments
  profitMarginPercent Float @default(15)
  laborCost           Float @default(0)
  additionalCost      Float @default(0)
  discountPercent     Float @default(0)

  /// ─── COMPUTED SNAPSHOTS (written at calculation time) ───
  glassCost         Float  @default(0)   // computed glass cost
  accessoryCost     Float  @default(0)   // total accessories cost
  materialCost      Float  @default(0)   // total bar material cost (from cutting optimization)
  totalBarsUsed     Int    @default(0)   // total full bars purchased
  wastePercent      Float  @default(0)   // overall waste % from optimization

  status String @default("DRAFT")

  createdAt DateTime @default(now())
  updatedAt DateTime @updatedAt

  template      ProductTemplate  @relation(fields: [templateId], references: [id], onDelete: Restrict)
  color         Color            @relation(fields: [colorId], references: [id], onDelete: Restrict)
  cuttingResults CuttingResult[]

  @@index([templateId])
  @@index([colorId])
  @@map("estimation_projects")
}
```

> [!WARNING]
> **Breaking change**: The old `EstimationProject` had optional `refWidthMm`/`refHeightMm` and a `items` relation to `EstimationItem`. The new version replaces these with required parametric fields (`templateId`, `colorId`, `widthMm`, `heightMm`) and `CuttingResult` instead of manual `EstimationItem`.

---

#### 6. `CuttingResult` — Output of 1D Bin Packing

Each row represents one **full bar** purchased, with its list of cuts.

```prisma
model CuttingResult {
  id                  String @id @default(cuid())
  estimationProjectId String
  materialId          String

  /// Which Material this bar is for (e.g., "iS-0101 เฟรมบน-ล่าง")
  materialCode  String
  materialName  String

  /// Unit cost per full bar (from MaterialVariant for selected color)
  barUnitCost   Float
  /// Standard bar length (mm)
  barLengthMm   Int

  /// Number of full bars needed for this material
  barsRequired  Int

  /// JSON array of cut assignments per bar
  /// e.g., [{"barIndex":1,"cuts":[1965,1965],"used":3930,"waste":2070},...]
  cutDetails    String    // JSON serialized

  /// Aggregate waste for this material group
  totalUsedMm   Int
  totalWasteMm  Int
  wastePercent  Float

  createdAt DateTime @default(now())

  estimationProject EstimationProject @relation(fields: [estimationProjectId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
  material          Material          @relation(fields: [materialId], references: [id], onDelete: Restrict)

  @@index([estimationProjectId])
  @@map("cutting_results")
}
```

---

#### 7. Model Removal: `EstimationItem`

> [!CAUTION]
> The `EstimationItem` model will be **removed**. It represents the old "manual BOM line item" approach. Its responsibilities are now fully replaced by:
> - `TemplateComponent` (defines what to cut, via formulas)
> - `CuttingResult` (stores the optimized cutting output)
>
> **Data migration**: Any existing estimation items in the database will be lost. Since the app is in development (pre-production), this is acceptable. If you need to preserve old data, please let me know.

---

### Relation Additions to Existing Models

Two existing models need **new relations** added (no breaking changes to their fields):

```diff
 model Category {
   ...
   materials Material[]
+  templates ProductTemplate[]
   ...
 }

 model Material {
   ...
   estimationItems EstimationItem[]  // ← REMOVED
+  templateComponents TemplateComponent[]
+  cuttingResults     CuttingResult[]
   ...
 }

 model Color {
   ...
   variants MaterialVariant[]
+  projects EstimationProject[]
   ...
 }
```

