## Complete New Flow Diagram

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A["👤 User selects Template + Color"] --> B["📐 Inputs W × H (mm)"]
    B --> C["⚙️ Formula Engine<br/>(Step 2)"]
    C --> D["📋 Cutting List Generated<br/>e.g., 4× 1965mm, 2× 965mm"]
    D --> E["📦 1D Bin Packing<br/>(Step 3 — FFD Algorithm)"]
    E --> F["🧮 Bar Calculation<br/>e.g., 3 full bars @ 6000mm"]
    
    C --> G["🪟 Glass Area Calculation<br/>panelCount × glassW × glassH"]
    
    F --> H["💰 Cost Computation"]
    G --> H
    I["🔩 Accessories<br/>(fixed per template)"] --> H
    
    H --> J["📄 Final Quotation<br/>Material + Glass + Accessories<br/>+ Margin + Labor"]
```

---

## Formula Engine Safety Design (Preview for Step 2)

| Concern | Solution |
|---------|----------|
| Code injection | **No `eval()`** — custom tokenizer + recursive-descent parser |
| Allowed tokens | `0-9`, `.`, `W`, `H`, `+`, `-`, `*`, `/`, `(`, `)` |
| Validation | Formula validated at template creation time AND at evaluation time |
| Error handling | Invalid formulas return descriptive errors, never crash |
| Precision | All arithmetic in standard JS `number` (IEEE 754 double — sufficient for mm) |

---

## Open Questions

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Q1: Bar Length Variation** — Do different profiles within the same template ever come in different stock lengths? (e.g., tracks = 6000mm but frames = 5800mm). The schema supports per-component `barLengthMm` override, but I want to confirm this is needed.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Q2: Kerf / Blade Width** — Should the cutting optimization account for saw blade kerf (typically 3-5mm per cut)? This affects how many cuts fit in a single bar. I can add a `kerfMm` field to `ProductTemplate` if needed.

> [!IMPORTANT]  
> **Q3: Existing Data** — The database currently has one sample estimation project with manual BOM items. Dropping the `EstimationItem` model will lose this data. Is that acceptable for this development pivot?

